<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Combat Extended compat: mirror CE's injury overhaul onto our two ragged wounds.

       CE rewrites Core's Cut and Stab injuries BY DEFNAME (Patches/Core/HediffDefs/
       Hediffs_Local_Injuries.xml, CE 16.7.4.0): the instant-roll HediffCompProperties_Infecter
       becomes CombatExtended.HediffCompProperties_InfecterCE (a per-hour-untended chance that
       scales with wound severity, triples on an inner part, and is divided by tend quality cubed,
       the mechanism every CE injury shares), Cut's scar factor drops to 0.75, and Stab's
       painPerSeverity rises to 0.0175. UMW_Cut_Ragged and UMW_Stab_Ragged are parentless clones of
       those two (their headers: Core's Cut and Stab carry no Name= to inherit from), so CE's patch
       never reaches them; without this file a ragged wound would be the only injury in a CE game
       still rolling vanilla's instant infection, and a ragged stab would hurt LESS than CE's clean
       one. CE's Stabilize comp needs no mirror: CE adds it to @Name="InjuryBase", which both clones
       inherit, and list nodes merge. Bleed rates need none either: CE leaves Cut and Stab at 0.06,
       so the clones' 0.12 stays the 2x the traits are built on (bleeding as a whole is far deadlier
       under CE through its body-part bleed multipliers, which hit clean and ragged wounds alike).

       - Infection: CE's own Cut (0.015/h) and Stab (0.03/h) rates, verbatim. The vanilla clones keep
         Core's 0.15 untouched because infection is not part of the ragged identity; same here.
       - UMW_Cut_Ragged scar factor 10 -> 7.5: the identity is "scars ten times the clean wound",
         and the clean cut is 0.75 under CE. UMW_Stab_Ragged stays at 10 because CE leaves Stab's
         factor at 1.
       - UMW_Stab_Ragged painPerSeverity 0.0125 -> 0.0175, CE's Stab value. Cut is unchanged in CE,
         so UMW_Cut_Ragged keeps 0.0125.

       The other on-hit payloads were audited against CE the same session (2026-11-03) and need no
       hediff work: BellCast's StunFor and DeadBlow's StaggerFor bypass the damage-stun path CE
       rewrites (StunHandler.Notify_DamageApplied; StaggerHandler is untouched); BloodStained's
       PanicFlee is a vanilla mental state CE never patches; UMW_SedativeBuildup is ours alone, and
       CE's Pawn_HealthTracker.CheckForStateChange transpiler removes vanilla's random death-on-downed
       roll, so an Opiated capture is strictly safer under CE. Envenomed and ZeusHeaded ride
       mechanics CE does overhaul (its wound-borne venom, its Electric armor and re-stun model); the
       findings sit in WeaponTraits_CE.xml's header beside the PlasmaCored retune. -->

  <!-- UMW_Cut_Ragged: CE's Cut infection model and a scar factor that stays 10x CE's Cut. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/HediffDef[defName="UMW_Cut_Ragged"]/comps/li[@Class="HediffCompProperties_Infecter"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="CombatExtended.HediffCompProperties_InfecterCE">
        <infectionChancePerHourUntended>0.015</infectionChancePerHourUntended>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/HediffDef[defName="UMW_Cut_Ragged"]/comps/li[@Class="HediffCompProperties_GetsPermanent"]/becomePermanentChanceFactor</xpath>
    <value>
      <becomePermanentChanceFactor>7.5</becomePermanentChanceFactor>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- UMW_Stab_Ragged: CE's Stab infection model and pain. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/HediffDef[defName="UMW_Stab_Ragged"]/comps/li[@Class="HediffCompProperties_Infecter"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="CombatExtended.HediffCompProperties_InfecterCE">
        <infectionChancePerHourUntended>0.03</infectionChancePerHourUntended>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/HediffDef[defName="UMW_Stab_Ragged"]/injuryProps/painPerSeverity</xpath>
    <value>
      <painPerSeverity>0.0175</painPerSeverity>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
